    <detaileddescription>
<para>This is used in place of actual DbgOps inside of a <ref refid="class_live_debug_values_1_1_dbg_value" kindref="compound">DbgValue</ref> to reduce its size, as <ref refid="class_live_debug_values_1_1_dbg_value" kindref="compound">DbgValue</ref> is very frequently used and passed around, and the actual <ref refid="struct_live_debug_values_1_1_dbg_op" kindref="compound">DbgOp</ref> is over 8x larger than this class, due to storing a <ref refid="classllvm_1_1_machine_operand" kindref="compound">MachineOperand</ref>. This ID should be equal for all equal DbgOps, and also encodes whether the mapped <ref refid="struct_live_debug_values_1_1_dbg_op" kindref="compound">DbgOp</ref> is a constant, meaning that for simple equality or const-ness checks it is not necessary to lookup this ID. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
